diff --git a/docs/specs/USB-PREARM-bench.md b/docs/specs/USB-PREARM-bench.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a7439ef
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/specs/USB-PREARM-bench.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# USB IN prearm experimental bench
+
+New Community OS behaviour, Level C: keep both isochronous IN descriptors armed.
+Intent: tolerate two host frame polls before the USB interrupt services completion.
+Each descriptor owns its own 992-byte InPacketBuffer until completion.
+Keep PingPong ownership, reset/alt-stop and feedback handling unchanged.
+Refill work is bounded by two packets per call; the existing ISR token loop stays bounded at 16.
+The second queued packet adds about one USB frame of buffering and one silent startup packet.
+No persistent formats, descriptors, audio sample clock or product UI change.
+Acceptance: the existing 12 iso tests plus known-data delayed-IRQ recovery pass for P2/P4/P6/P8/P10/P11.
+Acceptance: focused USB suites pass on host and Cortex-M4F QEMU; new regression is explicitly registered.
+Acceptance: two fresh MinSizeRel MK66 builds, rate44100 ON, audio-test OFF, produce identical verified HEX.
+Budget: one additional 992-byte packet buffer, actual alignment delta measured; preserve 32 KiB above the 24 KiB stack.
+Gate: target full ctest, image/flashconfig/link/ramfunc/noinit checks pass without warnings.
+Hardware pending: CPU/ISR peak, underruns, capture loss in capture/duplex, start/stop/re-enumeration.
+Bench only: gated image may be tested on the authorized unit; no merge, remote push or publishing.
